---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { legal } from '../../config/legal';
---

<LegalLayout lang="en" title="Privacy notice" alternates={{ it: '/privacy/', en: '/en/privacy/' }}>
  <p>
    This notice explains what personal data we collect through this website, why, and how we handle it, under
    Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    {legal.owner}, {legal.address}. For any privacy question, write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Request form</strong>: name, email, the period you are interested in, number of adults and children,
      country, your message and your choice about updates.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data</strong>: the provider hosting this website automatically logs data such as your IP address
      and browser type, for security and to keep the site running.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Statistics</strong>: if enabled, we count visits in aggregate form, without cookies and without
      identifying you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      To answer your request and send you the programme and a quote: a pre-contractual step you asked for (Art. 6(1)(b)
      GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      To send you news about upcoming seasons, only if you ticked the box: based on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR),
      which you can withdraw at any time.
    </li>
    <li>To keep the website secure: based on our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Information requests: up to 24 months from our last contact. If a request becomes a booking, data is kept for as
      long as the law requires.
    </li>
    <li>Updates: until you withdraw your consent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who can see it</h2>
  <p>
    Only the people on our team who answer requests, and the technical providers that help us run the website, acting
    as data processors. We never sell or share your data with anyone else.
  </p>
  {
    legal.processors.length > 0 && (
      <ul>
        {legal.processors.map((p) => (
          <li>
            {p.name}: {p.role.en}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )
  }
  <p>
    Some providers may be based outside the European Union, for example in the United States. In that case data is
    transferred with the safeguards required by the GDPR, such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or the European
    Commission's standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use profiling cookies or third-party cookies. Fonts are hosted on the website itself, with no
    connection to external services.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask at any time to access your data, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to its use, receive it in a
    portable format, or withdraw your consent. Just write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe your data is being handled unlawfully, you can lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection
    authority, the <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" rel="noopener">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a
    >, or with the authority in your own country.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
